Q: How does a Spring Boot application start?

Ordered mental model (interview):

main()
 → SpringApplication.run(...)
 → create ApplicationContext
 → auto-configure + component-scan + load properties
 → create/inject beans
 → start embedded server (web apps)
 → app ready (port 8080 by default)

────────────────────────────────────────
1) Main class + @SpringBootApplication

@SpringBootApplication = 
@Configuration + @EnableAutoConfiguration + @ComponentScan

public static void main(String[] args) {
    SpringApplication.run(MyApp.class, args);
}

────────────────────────────────────────
2) What SpringApplication.run() does (simplified)

1. Create `SpringApplication`
2. Prepare Environment (profiles, application.properties/yml, env vars, args)
3. Create ApplicationContext (AnnotationConfigServletWebServerApplicationContext for web)
4. Load bean definitions
5. Refresh context:
   - component scan (main package + subpackages)
   - auto-configuration (based on classpath starters)
   - create singleton beans + DI
6. If web: start embedded Tomcat/Jetty/Undertow
7. Call runners (`ApplicationRunner` / `CommandLineRunner`) if any
8. Publish ready events → app accepting traffic

────────────────────────────────────────
3) Auto-configuration

Sees jars on classpath, e.g.:
- spring-boot-starter-web → DispatcherServlet, Tomcat, MVC
- spring-boot-starter-data-jpa → DataSource, EntityManagerFactory, etc.

You can override with your own beans/properties.

────────────────────────────────────────
4) Component scanning

Finds `@Component` / `@Service` / `@Repository` / `@Controller` under the main class package tree and registers them as beans.

────────────────────────────────────────
5) Externalized config

Loads `application.properties` / `application.yml` (+ profile-specific files).
Applies to DataSource, server.port, logging, custom `@Value` / `@ConfigurationProperties`.

────────────────────────────────────────
6) Startup complete

Context is up, beans ready, embedded server listening (web).
Default: http://localhost:8080

────────────────────────────────────────
Interview one-liner

“Spring Boot starts from main with SpringApplication.run, builds the ApplicationContext, loads properties,
scans components, applies auto-configuration from the classpath, wires beans, starts the embedded server for web apps, then the application is ready to serve requests.”
